<title>BELGIUM: Lernout &amp; Hauspie makes profit in Q3 1996.</title>
<headline>Lernout &amp; Hauspie makes profit in Q3 1996.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Third quarter 1996 earnings</p>
<p>(million dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net income				     1.64 vs  2.58 loss</p>
<p>Earnings per share - primary (dollars) 0.11 vs  0.35 loss</p>
<p>    EPS - fully diluted (dollars)	    0.10 vs n/a</p>
<p>NOTE: Lernout &amp; Hauspie Speech Products is a Belgian Nasdaq-quoted company specialised in speech products technology.  </p>
<p>    Net revenues				   7.25 vs  2.09</p>
<p>    Cost of revenues			     1.27 vs  0.72</p>
<p>    Gross profit				   5.98 vs  1.37</p>
<p>    Operating expenses			   4.48 vs  3.48</p>
<p>    Income from operations		     1.50 vs  2.11 loss</p>
<p>NOTE - Lernout &amp; Hauspie said in a statement it also planned to issue in a few weeks convertible subordinated bonds over five years worth $50 million in a private placement.</p>
<p>It said it would use the biggest part of the net proceeds for strategic takeovers to strengthen its position in speech technology.</p>
<p>First nine months of 1996 (to Sept 30)</p>
<p>    Net income				     1.17 vs 11.30 loss</p>
<p>Earnings per share - primary (dollars) 0.08 vs  1.43 loss</p>
<p>    EPS - fully diluted (dollars)	    0.07 vs  n/a</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
